<description>&lt;p&gt;Violent clashes persist between Viv Ansanm gangs and Haitian security forces, now reinforced by a Kenya-led multinational mission patrolling Port-au-Prince and Kenscoff. The Dominican army has supplied large ammunition stocks to the 400 Mawozo gang, increasing its firepower against security forces. Erik Prince is operating an anti-gang mercenary effort in Haiti, adding a private-security dimension to the conflict. The United Nations has allocated an additional US$75 million for aid, supplementing earlier funding. The UCDP recorded 193 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMicEFVX3lxTFAwbnAyelpRcHBMS3VndVdfWXFtZXl2d0hoSjVqTnVQSjlPREpSYzE0TFZnV1Zkc3lNRll5MUhGMXpJdjN3U1B2V0RtbnR2Q2VmWEZDMHhVRUMzOFFDZ2lvYlp6WVJSejYzaUF4WEQ1SlU?oc=5&quot;&gt;CNN&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipwFBVV95cUxNZUQwWXpVMHR6Q1AxNFUwMGV5Rnc0XzhzN21LUDVWaUZQTEp3QUdtYVFIRy1FUFdJdXJTejA1V010UlBib004TEtjU1RWeXVNRHhCTmFRdndHQ1lsZzVYZEtZdXBDLUlINDVEbm1kQ2NkR05GTnB3R2toN1VJRFUtRVRFWi1XXy02d1FBRElzak5tYTFnZWJVMDBEVDMyY3ZnMXBSNW90OA?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMifkFVX3lxTE1PSDNZYklwbFlURFR4ZWw5TXBzM2kxUUV5SEZfZHFESFdkUVU2Q2tKUHZJSzBNeFNGZmlfTUQtb0pzaFJZNllRRjNMajF1RkJBdkNkcGF4aHVabFF4TzNteUhEQWVsazkxMnhJeFdSZVZfekluWW8xZjJSX2VYQQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Trinidad Guardian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqAFBVV95cUxQWWI2M0QzRHJ4MGNVdDFxTVNMazZCZ19IR25rZ1lyQi1yMVFnVTJrLVRfb2ZJLTBmbEEzQWczRXo5bGdidG5JaDByR21NS25yYWJYVE1jOGl5azZfWTV0Wi1xQVRZcVFuU1dKeExuUWpZNnBMQng3OThoRmpUcnBaVGR2MnI1M0ZXTF94QzVRV3A1M3o4TUY5WVQzZ2NfWndTTUlodjdLS3E?oc=5&quot;&gt;Caribbean National Weekly&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a